    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_c508152f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes two unrelated images: a child presenting flowers to a dignitary, and a kangaroo drinking beer. The text \"how to remember kid in hot car keep 2nd road beer with them!\" is a nonsensical, poorly constructed pun attempting to create a mnemonic. The intent is to humorously suggest a bizarre, illogical association (kangaroo drinking beer) to remember a serious safety issue (child in hot car). While not overtly abusive or hateful, the meme's humor relies on absurdity and potentially trivializes a dangerous real-world problem. The \"beer with them\" part is a crude, non-sequitur attempt at a mnemonic, which could be seen as harmful by implying that the only way to remember is through an inappropriate or trivial association, potentially undermining the seriousness of child safety. The kangaroo image is not used to target any specific group but is simply a visual gag.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_61aabf99"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
